---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "What are the main parts of CELPIP Listening?",
    answer:
      "The CELPIP Listening test includes problem solving, daily life conversation, information, news, discussion, and viewpoints sections.",
  },
  {
    question: "Should I listen the same way in every CELPIP Listening part?",
    answer:
      "No. Some parts reward fast practical listening, while others need stronger attention to opinion, attitude, or speaker purpose.",
  },
  {
    question: "What helps CELPIP Listening scores improve fastest?",
    answer:
      "Scores usually improve faster when students learn the section patterns, predict what kind of answer they need, and stop leaving questions blank.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "CELPIP Listening Question Types Guide", path: "/blog/celpip-listening-question-types/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="CELPIP Listening Question Types Guide | Strategies for Every Part"
  description="A practical CELPIP Listening guide with section-by-section strategy for problem solving, conversation, information, news, discussion, and viewpoints."
  type="article"
  keywords="CELPIP listening question types, CELPIP listening strategy, CELPIP listening tips"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section guide-article">
    <a class="guide-back-link" href="/blog">Back to blog</a>

    <header class="guide-header">
      <span class="guide-tag">CELPIP listening guide</span>
      <h1 style="margin: 0;">CELPIP Listening question types</h1>
      <div class="guide-meta">
        <span>March 17, 2026</span>
        <span>7 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-lead">
      <p>
        CELPIP Listening rewards pattern recognition. Each section sounds different and asks
        you to notice different things, so one general listening strategy is not enough.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once you know what each part is testing, the questions feel much more predictable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="guide-card">
      <h2>The six listening parts</h2>
      <div class="guide-grid guide-grid-2">
        <div class="guide-card">
          <h3>Part 1: Problem solving</h3>
          <p class="muted">Listen for the practical decision, not only for background details.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-card">
          <h3>Part 2: Daily life conversation</h3>
          <p class="muted">Track who says what and why the conversation is happening.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-card">
          <h3>Part 3: Information</h3>
          <p class="muted">Notice key facts, sequence, and instructions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-card">
          <h3>Part 4: News item</h3>
          <p class="muted">Focus on the main event, cause, and result.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-card">
          <h3>Part 5: Discussion</h3>
          <p class="muted">Watch each speaker's opinion and how it changes during the talk.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-card">
          <h3>Part 6: Viewpoints</h3>
          <p class="muted">Separate the writer's or speaker's attitude from supporting details.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Best habits for every section</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>Read the choices quickly before the audio begins.</li>
        <li>Predict what kind of information you need.</li>
        <li>Keep moving forward because you cannot go back later.</li>
        <li>Never leave a question blank.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Where students often lose marks</h2>
      <table class="guide-mistake-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Problem</th>
          <th>Better move</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>They focus on one detail and miss the main point.</td>
          <td>Ask what the speaker is trying to decide, explain, or recommend.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>They do not notice changes in opinion.</td>
          <td>Listen for contrast words like but, however, actually, and instead.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>They leave blanks and plan to return later.</td>
          <td>Choose the best answer before time moves you forward.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>They treat every section like the same kind of task.</td>
          <td>Adjust your focus based on whether the part is factual, practical, or opinion-based.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Next step</h2>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="/blog/celpip-reading-question-types">
          <strong>Read the CELPIP reading guide</strong>
          <span>Study the reading patterns that often match the same practical skills.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/celpip/listening">
          <strong>Go to the CELPIP listening hub</strong>
          <span>Open the main listening page for lessons and more strategy.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/celpip/listening">
          <strong>Study CELPIP listening lessons</strong>
          <span>Practice the language and skills behind each listening part.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <div class="guide-faq">
        {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="card">
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <section class="section-sm" style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center;">
    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin-bottom: var(--s-5);" />
    <p class="muted">Want a CLB 9 writing system you can actually follow?</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/celpip/writing">Get the system</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
